int, teste e build.",["Date","2026-02-03T00:00:00.000Z"],false,"## Workflow mínimo\n\n```yaml\nname: CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  pull_request:\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n      - run: npm ci\n      - run: npm run build\n```\n\n## Boas práticas\n\n- Fixar versões das actions por hash ou tag confiável.\n- Rodar lint e testes antes do build para falhar rápido.\n- Usar cache de dependências para acelerar o pipeline.","src/content/posts/ci-cd/pipeline-com-github-actions.md","c41431886b44ad37",{"html":22,"metadata":23},"\u003Ch2 id=\"workflow-mínimo\">Workflow mínimo\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cpre class=\"astro-code github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8; overflow-x: auto;\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"yaml\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">name\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">CI\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#79B8FF\">on\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">  push\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">    branches\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: [\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">main\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">  pull_request\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">jobs\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">  build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">    runs-on\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">ubuntu-latest\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">    steps\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">      - \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">uses\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">actions/checkout@v4\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">      - \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">uses\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">actions/setup-node@v4\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">        with\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">          node-version\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#79B8FF\">22\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">      - \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">npm ci\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">      - \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">npm run build\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"boas-práticas\">Boas práticas\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Fixar versões das actions por hash ou tag confiável.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Rodar lint e testes antes do build para falhar rápido.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Usar cache de dependências para acelerar o pipeline.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n",{"headings":24,"localImagePaths":32,"remoteImagePaths":33,"frontmatter":34,"imagePaths":36},[25,29],{"depth":26,"slug":27,"text":28},2,"workflow-mínimo","Workflow mínimo",{"depth":26,"slug":30,"text":31},"boas-práticas","Boas práticas",[],[],{"title":14,"description":15,"date":35},["Date","2026-02-03T00:00:00.000Z"],[],"kubernetes/introducao-a-pods",{"id":37,"data":39,"body":43,"filePath":44,"digest":45,"rendered":46},{"title":40,"description":41,"date":42,"draft":17},"Introdução a Pods no Kubernetes","O que é um Pod, por que ele é a menor unidade de deploy e como isso afeta o design de aplicações.",["Date","2026-01-15T00:00:00.000Z"],"## O que é um Pod?\n\nUm **Pod** é a menor unidade de execução no Kubernetes. Ele agrupa um ou mais containers que\ncompartilham rede e armazenamento.\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: nginx-exemplo\nspec:\n  containers:\n    - name: nginx\n      image: nginx:1.27\n```\n\n### Por que não rodar containers direto?\n\nO Kubernetes precisa de uma unidade que possa carregar metadados de agendamento, rede e ciclo\nde vida — o Pod resolve isso, mesmo quando só existe um container dentro dele.\n\n> Na prática, a maioria dos Pods em produção tem exatamente um container principal, mas o\n> modelo permite sidecars (proxy, log shipper, etc).","src/content/posts/kubernetes/introducao-a-pods.md","ec65f8710b40d9de",{"html":47,"metadata":48},"\u003Ch2 id=\"o-que-é-um-pod\">O que é um Pod?\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Um \u003Cstrong>Pod\u003C/strong> é a menor unidade de execução no Kubernetes. Ele agrupa um ou mais containers que\ncompartilham rede e armazenamento.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"astro-code github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8; overflow-x: auto;\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"yaml\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">apiVersion\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">v1\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">kind\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">Pod\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">metadata\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">  name\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">nginx-exemplo\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">spec\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">  containers\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">    - \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">name\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">nginx\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#85E89D\">      image\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">nginx:1.27\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Ch3 id=\"por-que-não-rodar-containers-direto\">Por que não rodar containers direto?\u003C/h3>\n\u003Cp>O Kubernetes precisa de uma unidade que possa carregar metadados de agendamento, rede e ciclo\nde vida — o Pod resolve isso, mesmo quando só existe um container dentro dele.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cblockquote>\n\u003Cp>Na prática, a maioria dos Pods em produção tem exatamente um container principal, mas o\nmodelo permite sidecars (proxy, log shipper, etc).\u003C/p>\n\u003C/blockquote>\n",{"headings":49,"localImagePaths":57,"remoteImagePaths":58,"frontmatter":59,"imagePaths":61},[50,53],{"depth":26,"slug":51,"text":52},"o-que-é-um-pod","O que é um Pod?",{"depth":54,"slug":55,"text":56},3,"por-que-não-rodar-containers-direto","Por que não rodar containers direto?",[],[],{"title":40,"description":41,"date":60},["Date","2026-01-15T00:00:00.000Z"],[]]